    "collapsible_tabs_G7jT6N": {
      "type": "collapsible-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "question_7JcbVB": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What should I consider when buying an ergonomic chair?",
            "answer": "<p>When choosing an ergonomic chair, consider factors such as adjustability (seat height, lumbar support, armrests), the material (mesh for breathability, padding for comfort), and your personal needs (office work, gaming, or study). You can use our comparison tables to see the key differences between SIHOO models.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_WKEGzF": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Which SIHOO chair is best for long working hours?",
            "answer": "<p>For extended sitting periods, we recommend models like the SIHOO M18, M57, C300, or S300. These chairs feature breathable mesh backs, W-shaped cushions, and fully adjustable lumbar support, ensuring you stay comfortable and supported throughout the day.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_back_pain": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Which SIHOO chair is best for back pain?",
            "answer": "<p>Chairs with dynamic, self-adjusting lumbar support work best for lower-back pain because the support follows you as you move. In the Doro range, the Doro C300 Pro V2 and Doro S300 have the most advanced lumbar systems; in the M series the M57 Pro and M18 offer adjustable lumbar support at a lower price. If your pain is mostly in the neck and shoulders, choose a model with an adjustable headrest such as the M57, M18 Pro or any Doro chair. Read our guide to the <a href=\"/blogs/reviews/best-ergonomic-chair-for-lower-back-pain-in-australia-2026-guide\">best ergonomic chair for lower back pain in Australia</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_doro_vs_m": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is the difference between the Doro series and the M series?",
            "answer": "<p>The Doro series is SIHOO's premium range: self-adjusting dynamic lumbar support, a weight-sensing or self-adaptive recline mechanism, a longer 5-year warranty and design awards such as the German Design Award and Red Dot. The M series (M18, M57, M59, M90 and others) covers the essentials – breathable mesh, adjustable lumbar, headrest and armrests, 150 kg rating – at a lower price with a 3-year warranty. If you sit for six or more hours a day, the Doro chairs are worth the step up; for a home office or study desk the M series is excellent value.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_gaming_vs_office": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Should I buy a gaming chair or an ergonomic office chair?",
            "answer": "<p>For long sessions an ergonomic mesh office chair usually wins: it breathes better in the Australian climate and supports a neutral posture. Our XALLKING X5 and X3 gaming chairs combine the racing-style look with proper ergonomics – adjustable lumbar, 4D armrests and a full recline – so you do not have to choose. See <a href=\"/blogs/all-about-ergonomic-chair/gaming-chair-vs-ergonomic-office-chair-for-spine-health\">gaming chair vs ergonomic office chair for spine health</a>.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
