      "type": "collapsible-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "question_zbFaDG": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are SIHOO chairs suitable for taller or shorter individuals?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, SIHOO chairs are designed to accommodate a wide range of body types. With adjustable seat height, depth, and lumbar support, our chairs can be tailored to fit people of various heights. For specific measurements, please check the product dimensions listed in the descriptions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_tall": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Which SIHOO chair is best for tall people?",
            "answer": "<p>If you are over 185 cm, look for a taller backrest, a longer seat-depth range and a headrest that lifts high: the Doro C300 Pro V2, Doro S300, Doro C500, M57 Pro and M18 Pro all suit users up to 190 cm. Each product page lists the recommended user height range under Specifications. Our guide to the <a href=\"/blogs/reviews/ergonomic-chair-for-tall-people\">best office chair for tall people in Australia</a> compares the options.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_short": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Which SIHOO chair suits shorter users?",
            "answer": "<p>Users under about 160 cm should choose a chair with a low minimum seat height (around 40–43 cm) and adjustable seat depth so the front edge does not press behind the knees. The M76, M57 Pro, M59 and M18 have the lowest seat heights in our range. A footrest can also help if your feet do not sit flat on the floor.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
